<p>Many online platforms list rental properties in Eindhoven. These include:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><a href="https://www.funda.nl/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener nofollow">Funda</a></li>



<li><a href="https://housinganywhere.com/Netherlands?utm_source=expatica&amp;utm_medium=affiliate&amp;affiliate_partner_id=975640" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener sponsored nofollow">HousingAnywhere</a></li>



<li><a href="https://jdt8.net/c/?si=17650&amp;li=1767268&amp;wi=344199&amp;ws=" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener sponsored nofollow">Huurwoningen</a></li>



<li><a href="https://kamernet.nl/en" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener nofollow">Kamernet</a></li>



<li><a href="https://www.pararius.com/english" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener nofollow">Pararius</a></li>
</ul>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="typical-accommodation">Typical accommodation in Eindhoven</h3>



<p>As Eindhoven continues to expand its housing developments, many residents live in fairly new buildings. The city offers both apartments, especially towards <em>Centrum</em> (the city center), but also independent houses. </p>



<p>Students usually rent a room in an apartment or stay in university residences on campus. The housing market is competitive, so make sure you give yourself at least a few months for your accommodation search, whether renting or buying.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="renting">Renting in Eindhoven</h3>



<p>Renting in Eindhoven is similar to <a href="https://www.expatica.com/nl/housing/renting/renting-a-property-in-the-netherlands-102925/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">renting in other Dutch cities</a>. Apartments and single-family homes are the most common type of property to rent, and prices depend on the property&#8217;s size, location, and condition. A standalone house in Elzent, just south of the city center, will fetch more than the more affordable Eikenburg, for example.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1800" height="1200" src="https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/canal-eindhoven.jpg" alt="Residential building next to a canal in Eindhoven" class="wp-image-7576" srcset="https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/canal-eindhoven.jpg 1800w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/canal-eindhoven-300x200.jpg 300w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/canal-eindhoven-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/canal-eindhoven-768x512.jpg 768w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/canal-eindhoven-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/canal-eindhoven-380x253.jpg 380w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1800px) 100vw, 1800px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Photo: Alicja Ziaj/Unsplash</figcaption></figure>



<p>When finding a property to rent, you first arrange to view the property, then express your interest and, if chosen, sign the contract. You must also typically pay a two-month deposit.</p>



<p>When securing your rental property, you&#8217;ll likely need to transfer your deposit and first month&#8217;s rent internationally. Many expats use payment institutions like <a href="https://wise.com/nl/send-money/?utm_source=expatica-com&amp;utm_medium=affiliate&amp;utm_campaign=guides&amp;utm_content=be/moving/location/https://wise.com/be/account/?utm_source=expatica-com&amp;utm_medium=affiliate&amp;utm_campaign=guides&amp;utm_content=nl/moving/location/where-to-live-in-eindhoven-100616" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wise</a> to send money to the Netherlands, as these services use the mid-market exchange rate—the real exchange rate without markup—alongside transparent fees. This can be particularly helpful when you need to manage EUR expenses while still holding funds in your home currency. Be sure to review the <a href="https://wise.com/nl/pricing/?utm_source=expatica-com&amp;utm_medium=affiliate&amp;utm_campaign=guides&amp;utm_content=nl/moving/location/https://wise.com/be/account/?utm_source=expatica-com&amp;utm_medium=affiliate&amp;utm_campaign=guides&amp;utm_content=be/moving/location/where-to-live-in-eindhoven-100616" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">fee structure</a> before making your transfer to understand the total cost.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="buying">Buying in Eindhoven</h3>



<p>If you plan to stay in the Netherlands long-term, you may consider <a href="https://admin.expatica.com/nl/housing/buying/buying-a-property-in-the-netherlands-100633/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">buying</a>. When purchasing a home in Eindhoven, the easiest way is to hire a real estate agent (<em>makelaar</em>). They can assist you when looking for a property and guide you through the entire buying process.</p>



<div class="interal-link-wrapper">
            <div class="img-left">
            <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/11/buying-a-home-in-the-netherlands.jpg"  alt="#" width="217" height="144">
        </div>
            <a href="https://www.expatica.com/nl/housing/buying/buying-a-property-in-the-netherlands-100633/" aria-label="Housing Buying a home in the Netherlands" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
