"de","Expatica Germany","https://admin.expatica.com/de/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2023/10/de.svg","Germany",{"blog_id":464,"domain":412,"code":465,"name":466,"country_flag":467,"country_site_name":468},"40","id","Expatica Indonesia","https://admin.expatica.com/id/wp-content/uploads/sites/40/2026/07/id.svg","Indonesia",{"blog_id":470,"domain":412,"code":471,"name":472,"country_flag":473,"country_site_name":474},"17","it","Expatica Italy","https://admin.expatica.com/it/wp-content/uploads/sites/17/2023/10/it.svg","Italy",{"blog_id":476,"domain":412,"code":477,"name":478,"country_flag":479,"country_site_name":480},"18","jp","Expatica Japan","https://admin.expatica.com/jp/wp-content/uploads/sites/18/2023/10/jp.svg","Japan",{"blog_id":482,"domain":412,"code":483,"name":484,"country_flag":485,"country_site_name":486},"7","lu","Expatica Luxembourg","https://admin.expatica.com/lu/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2023/10/lu.svg","Luxembourg",{"blog_id":488,"domain":412,"code":489,"name":490,"country_flag":491,"country_site_name":492},"3","nl","Expatica Netherlands","https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/10/nl.svg","Netherlands",{"blog_id":494,"domain":412,"code":495,"name":496,"country_flag":497,"country_site_name":498},"8","pt","Expatica Portugal","https://admin.expatica.com/pt/wp-content/uploads/sites/8/2023/10/pt.svg","Portugal",{"blog_id":500,"domain":412,"code":501,"name":502,"country_flag":503,"country_site_name":504},"33","pt-pt","Expatica Portugal (PT)","https://admin.expatica.com/pt-pt/wp-content/uploads/sites/33/2023/10/pt.svg","Portugal (Português)",{"blog_id":506,"domain":412,"code":507,"name":508,"country_flag":509,"country_site_name":510},"13","qa","Expatica Qatar","https://admin.expatica.com/qa/wp-content/uploads/sites/13/2023/10/qa.svg","Qatar",{"blog_id":512,"domain":412,"code":513,"name":514,"country_flag":515,"country_site_name":516},"11","ru","Expatica Russia","https://admin.expatica.com/ru/wp-content/uploads/sites/11/2023/10/ru.svg","Russia",{"blog_id":518,"domain":412,"code":519,"name":520,"country_flag":521,"country_site_name":522},"14","sa","Expatica Saudi Arabia","https://admin.expatica.com/sa/wp-content/uploads/sites/14/2023/10/sa.svg","Saudi Arabia",{"blog_id":524,"domain":412,"code":525,"name":526,"country_flag":527,"country_site_name":528},"24","sg","Expatica Singapore","https://admin.expatica.com/sg/wp-content/uploads/sites/24/2025/11/sg-1.svg","Singapore",{"blog_id":530,"domain":412,"code":531,"name":532,"country_flag":533,"country_site_name":534},"12","za","Expatica South Africa","https://admin.expatica.com/za/wp-content/uploads/sites/12/2023/10/za.svg","South Africa",{"blog_id":536,"domain":412,"code":537,"name":538,"country_flag":539,"country_site_name":540},"2","es","Expatica Spain","https://admin.expatica.com/es/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2023/10/es.svg","Spain",{"blog_id":542,"domain":412,"code":543,"name":544,"country_flag":545,"country_site_name":546},"9","ch","Expatica Switzerland","https://admin.expatica.com/ch/wp-content/uploads/sites/9/2023/10/ch.svg","Switzerland",{"blog_id":548,"domain":412,"code":549,"name":550,"country_flag":551,"country_site_name":552},"25","th","Expatica Thailand","https://admin.expatica.com/th/wp-content/uploads/sites/25/2024/03/022-thailand.svg","Thailand",{"blog_id":554,"domain":412,"code":555,"name":556,"country_flag":557,"country_site_name":558},"15","ae","Expatica United Arab Emirates","https://admin.expatica.com/ae/wp-content/uploads/sites/15/2023/10/ae.svg","United Arab Emirates",{"blog_id":560,"domain":412,"code":561,"name":562,"country_flag":563,"country_site_name":564},"10","uk","Expatica United Kingdom","https://admin.expatica.com/uk/wp-content/uploads/sites/10/2023/10/uk.svg","United Kingdom",{"blog_id":566,"domain":412,"code":567,"name":568,"country_flag":569,"country_site_name":570},"30","us","Expatica USA","https://admin.expatica.com/us/wp-content/uploads/sites/30/2025/10/us-1.svg","USA",{"blog_id":572,"domain":412,"code":573,"name":574,"country_flag":575,"country_site_name":576},"36","zh-us","Expatica美国","https://admin.expatica.com/zh-us/wp-content/uploads/sites/36/2026/04/us-1.svg","美国",{"blog_id":578,"domain":412,"code":579,"name":580,"country_flag":581,"country_site_name":582},"32","zh-my","Expatica马来西亚","https://admin.expatica.com/zh-my/wp-content/uploads/sites/32/2026/03/Flag_of_Malaysia.png","马来西亚",{"id":584,"title":585,"content":586,"modified":587,"topic":588,"articleTemplate":590,"standfirst":13,"reviewer":591,"outside":12,"authorInsideImage":592,"authorInside":593,"authorInsideSlug":594,"authorBiography":595,"authorSocials":596,"authorName":13,"authorImageUrl":591,"heroPlacements":597,"heroPlacementsMeta":598,"yoast_head_json":601,"link":629,"categories":671,"image":673},2538,"Where to live in Eindhoven","\n\u003Cp>Discover life in the technology and design hub of the Netherlands and explore the best places to live in Eindhoven.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>You may know Eindhoven for being the birthplace of Philips, but this vibrant and lively city has so much more to offer. Besides being a technology hub for businesses, it&#8217;s home to top design, a vibrant cultural scene, and a large student population. \u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Therefore, it&#8217;s no surprise that this city is a popular choice for expats. Whether you are working at one of its numerous tech companies or studying, Eindhoven has something for everyone. Find out about where to live when moving to Eindhoven in the following sections:\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cdiv class=\"wp-block-yoast-seo-table-of-contents yoast-table-of-contents\">\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"#overview\" data-level=\"2\">An overview of Eindhoven\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"#h-preparing-financially-for-your-move\" data-level=\"2\">Preparing financially for your move\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"#housing\" data-level=\"2\">How to find housing in Eindhoven\u003C/a>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"#typical-accommodation\" data-level=\"3\">Typical accommodation in Eindhoven\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"#renting\" data-level=\"3\">Renting in Eindhoven\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"#buying\" data-level=\"3\">Buying in Eindhoven\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"#neighborhoods\" data-level=\"2\">Neighborhoods in Eindhoven\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"#centrum-bergen\" data-level=\"2\">Centrum\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"#strijp\" data-level=\"2\">Strijp\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"#woensel\" data-level=\"2\">Woensel\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"#stratum\" data-level=\"2\">Stratum\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"#gestel\" data-level=\"2\">Gestel\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"#tongelre\" data-level=\"2\">Tongelre\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"#geldrop\" data-level=\"2\">Geldrop\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"#neighborhoods-to-avoid\" data-level=\"2\">Neighborhoods to avoid in Eindhoven\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"#tips\" data-level=\"2\">Tips on choosing a neighborhood in Eindhoven\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"#useful-resources\" data-level=\"2\">Useful resources\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003C/div>\n\n\n\u003Cdiv class=\"presentation-card\">\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"presentation-card-content\">\n        \u003Ch3 class=\"title\">ABN AMRO\u003C/h3>\n        \u003Cp class=\"description\">Are you an expat looking to buy a house in the Netherlands? While the process may be different from what you&#8217;re used to, ABN AMRO is here to help. You can use their online mortgage calculator or make an appointment with a mortgage advisor. With ABN AMRO, buying a house may be much easier than you thought.\u003C/p>\n                \u003Cdiv style=\"text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 8px;\">\n        \u003Ca href=\"https://www.abnamro.nl/en/personal/mortgages/applying-for-mortgage/mortgage-for-expats.html?utm_source=ExpaticaSP-100616\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored noopener\" class=\"read-more presentation-card__cta\">\n            \u003Cp style=\"white-space: nowrap; color:#000000;\" class=\"m-0 text-black\">Go to website\u003C/p>\n            \u003Cimg loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://admin.expatica.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/ico-external-link.svg\" width=\"12\" height=\"16\" class=\"boxout-img\" alt=\"\">\n        \u003C/a>\n\u003C/div>\n            \u003C/div>\n            \u003Cdiv\n          class=\"presentation-card-logo\"\n          style=\"background-image: url(https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2014/05/abn-amro-logo-200-white.png)\"\n        >\u003C/div>\n        \u003C/div>\n    \u003Cstyle>\n.presentation-card {\n  background-color: #F8F8F8;\n  border-radius: 16px;\n  padding: 55px;\n  margin-top: 56px;\n  margin-bottom: 56px;\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n}\n\n\n\n.presentation-card-content { \n  flex: 1;\n  max-width: 400px;\n}\n\n.presentation-card-content .label {\n    color: #00CBA8 !important;\n    font-size: 17px !important;\n    line-height: 20px !important;\n    margin-bottom: 5px !important;\n}\n\n.presentation-card-content .title {\n    font-size: 23px !important;\n    line-height: 40px !important;\n}\n\n.presentation-card-content .description {\n    color: #666666 !important;\n    font-size: 18px !important;\n    line-height: 32px !important;\n    margin-bottom: 30px !important;\n}\n\n.presentation-card-content .read-more {\n    color: #000000 !important;\n    font-family: 'Grold-Regular', 'Nunito Sans', 'Arial', 'sans-serif';\n    font-size: 19px !important;\n    line-height: 23px !important;\n    text-align: left !important;\n    text-decoration: none !important;\n    position: relative !important;\n    max-width: 140px;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n  } \n\n    /* .read-more::after {\n      position: absolute;\n      content: '';\n      width: 100% !important;\n      bottom: -5px !important;\n      background: #000000 !important;\n      height: 1px !important;\n      left: 0 !important;\n    } */\n\n.read-more img {\n    margin-left: 7px !important;\n    height: 20x !important;\n    width: 16px!important;\n}\n\n.presentation-card-logo {\n    flex: 2;\n    border-radius: 8px;\n    width: 150px;\n    max-width: 150px;\n    height: 150px;\n    background-repeat: no-repeat;\n    background-size: contain;\n    background-position: center;\n    background-color: #ECECEC;\n}\n\n.boxout-img {\n  height: 24px!important;\n}\n\n/* Media query for screens with width less than 769 pixels */\n@media screen and (max-width: 768px) {\n\n.presentation-card {\n    display: grid;\n    flex-flow: column-reverse;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n  padding-left: 35px!important;\n  padding-right: 35px!important;\n}\n\n.presentation-card-content { \n  max-width: 400px;\n  order: 2;\n}\n\n.presentation-card-content .title {\n    font-size: 23px !important;\n    line-height: 34px !important;\n}\n\n.presentation-card-content .description  {\n  font-size: 16px!important;\n}\n\n.presentation-card-logo {\n    order: 1;\n    border-radius: 8px;\n    width: 150px;\n    max-width: 150px;\n    height: 150px;\n    margin-bottom: 32px;\n    background-repeat: no-repeat;\n    background-size: contain;\n    background-position: center;\n    background-color: #ECECEC;\n}\n\n} \n\n\n/* --- 2026 partner-card additions ------------------------------------------\n   New classes only. Every selector above is untouched, so the classic card\n   renders byte-for-byte as before; these just keep the new optional elements\n   from landing unstyled on the classic template. The redesigned frontend\n   (.av2 scope) overrides all of them. */\n\n.presentation-card-content .presentation-card__bullets {\n    list-style: none !important;\n    margin: 0 0 28px !important;\n    padding: 0 !important;\n}\n\n.presentation-card-content .presentation-card__bullets li {\n    position: relative;\n    margin-bottom: 12px !important;\n    padding-left: 30px !important;\n    color: #1A2749 !important;\n    font-size: 16px !important;\n    line-height: 24px !important;\n}\n\n.presentation-card-content .presentation-card__bullets li:last-child {\n    margin-bottom: 0 !important;\n}\n\n.presentation-card-content .presentation-card__bullets li::before {\n    content: '';\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 0;\n    top: 3px;\n    width: 18px;\n    height: 18px;\n    border-radius: 50%;\n    background-color: #00CBA8;\n    background-image: url(\"data:image/svg+xml;charset=utf-8,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 24 24' fill='none' stroke='%23ffffff' stroke-width='3.5' stroke-linecap='round' stroke-linejoin='round'%3E%3Cpath d='M20 6 9 17l-5-5'/%3E%3C/svg%3E\");\n    background-repeat: no-repeat;\n    background-position: center;\n    background-size: 11px 11px;\n}\n\n.presentation-card-content .presentation-card__note {\n    margin: 12px 0 0 !important;\n    color: #666666 !important;\n    font-size: 14px !important;\n    line-height: 20px !important;\n}\n\n/* --- Bullet styles (bullets_style) ----------------------------------------\n   The bullet rules above are the \"ticks\" style and are left exactly as they\n   were. Numbers and bullet points only swap the marker. The ol is reset by\n   the shared .presentation-card__bullets rule (no list-style, no padding), and\n   its items drop their own markers so nothing fights the pseudo-element.\n\n   The !important flags are deliberate and kept to the minimum: the classic\n   article stylesheet draws its own custom bullet on every `ul li::before`\n   inside the article body (content \"\\2022\", position: relative, a 1em width\n   and a -1em margin) at far higher specificity than this block can reach.\n   Selectors stay at the block's usual (0,2,x) so the redesigned frontend can\n   still override all of it. */\n\n.presentation-card-content .presentation-card__bullets--numbers {\n    counter-reset: presentation-card-bullets;\n}\n\n.presentation-card-content .presentation-card__bullets--numbers li,\n.presentation-card-content .presentation-card__bullets--bullets li {\n    list-style: none !important;\n}\n\n.presentation-card-content .presentation-card__bullets--numbers li {\n    counter-increment: presentation-card-bullets;\n}\n\n/* Numbers: the tick's 18px teal disc, with a navy counter instead of the tick\n   (navy on #00CBA8 is ~7:1; white would be ~2:1 and fail text contrast). */\n.presentation-card-content .presentation-card__bullets--numbers li::before {\n    content: counter(presentation-card-bullets);\n    background-image: none;\n    color: #1A2749;\n    font-family: 'Lexend-Bold', 'Arial', sans-serif;\n    font-size: 11px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    line-height: 18px;\n    text-align: center;\n}\n\n/* Bullet points: a small teal dot, centred in the tick's 18px column and on\n   the item's 24px first line. */\n.presentation-card-content .presentation-card__bullets--bullets li::before {\n    content: '' !important;\n    position: absolute !important;\n    left: 5px;\n    top: 8px !important;\n    width: 8px !important;\n    height: 8px;\n    margin: 0 !important;\n    background-image: none;\n}\n\n\u003C/style>\n\n\n\n\u003Ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"overview\">An overview of Eindhoven\u003C/h2>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Eindhoven, the Netherlands&#8217; fifth-largest city, is located in North Brabant in the south of the Netherlands. Despite its southerly location, it&#8217;s well-connected by public transport and is home to Eindhoven Airport, the country&#8217;s second-largest airport.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>This city is ideal if you&#8217;re keen to live somewhere that blends modernity with a small-town feel. It&#8217;s home to many tech companies and startups ,which contrast with the charming architecture of the historic city center, such as Markt Square and Sint-Catharinkerk (St. Catherine&#8217;s Church).\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cfigure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\">\u003Cimg loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1800\" height=\"1200\" src=\"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/cycling-graffiti.jpg\" alt=\"A woman on a bike cycling past a mural in an underpass\" class=\"wp-image-7578\" srcset=\"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/cycling-graffiti.jpg 1800w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/cycling-graffiti-300x200.jpg 300w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/cycling-graffiti-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/cycling-graffiti-768x512.jpg 768w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/cycling-graffiti-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/cycling-graffiti-380x253.jpg 380w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1800px) 100vw, 1800px\" />\u003Cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Photo: Tayla Kohler/Unsplash\u003C/figcaption>\u003C/figure>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>With a population of almost \u003Ca href=\"https://www.statista.com/statistics/862755/total-population-of-eindhoven/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">250,000\u003C/a> and seven main districts, many expats also reside here. It has plenty of international companies and two universities: the Design Academy Eindhoven and Eindhoven University of Technology (TU Eindhoven).\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>The city is also famous for hosting the annual Dutch Design Week, one of the largest events of its kind in Europe.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-preparing-financially-for-your-move\">\u003Cstrong>Preparing financially for your move\u003C/strong>\u003C/h2>\n\n\n\n\u003Cfigure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\">\u003Cimg decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://admin.expatica.com/de/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2017/04/wise-account-40-currencies-euro-768x256-1.webp\" alt=\"Wise multi currency account offers 40+ currencies in one account.\" class=\"wp-image-6501\" loading=\"lazy\"/>\u003C/figure>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Moving to Belgium involves managing your finances across borders, from transferring rental deposits to paying monthly expenses in euros. When making international money transfers, it&#8217;s worth understanding the difference between the mid-market exchange rate and the rates typically offered by banks. The mid-market exchange rate is the midpoint between the buy and sell prices of two currencies—essentially the &#8220;true&#8221; exchange rate you see on financial news sites, with no markup added.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Payment institutions like \u003Ca href=\"https://wise.com/nl/account/?utm_source=expatica-com&amp;utm_medium=affiliate&amp;utm_campaign=guides&amp;utm_content=be/moving/location/https://wise.com/be/account/?utm_source=expatica-com&amp;utm_medium=affiliate&amp;utm_campaign=guides&amp;utm_content=nl/moving/location/where-to-live-in-eindhoven-100616\">Wise\u003C/a>, which is licensed by the National Bank of Belgium, use the mid-market exchange rate for international transfers with transparent, upfront fees. This means you can see exactly what you&#8217;re paying before you send money, helping you manage your finances more effectively during your move to Antwerp. You can check the \u003Ca href=\"https://wise.com/nl/pricing/?utm_source=expatica-com&amp;utm_medium=affiliate&amp;utm_campaign=guides&amp;utm_content=be/moving/location/https://wise.com/be/account/?utm_source=expatica-com&amp;utm_medium=affiliate&amp;utm_campaign=guides&amp;utm_content=nl/moving/location/where-to-live-in-eindhoven-100616\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">full fee structure on Wise&#8217;s website\u003C/a> to understand the costs involved in your specific transfer.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cdiv class=\"wp-block-expatica-cta-buttons flex flex-wrap items-center w-full font-grold-medium justify-center gap-4 mt-0 mb-4\">\n\u003Ca href=\"https://wise.com/nl/account/?utm_source=expatica-com&amp;utm_medium=affiliate&amp;utm_campaign=guides&amp;utm_content=be/moving/location/https://wise.com/be/account/?utm_source=expatica-com&amp;utm_medium=affiliate&amp;utm_campaign=guides&amp;utm_content=nl/moving/location/where-to-live-in-eindhoven-100616\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center text-center leading-none transition-colors duration-200 bg-[#00cba8] hover:bg-[#00b397] text-white rounded-xl font-bold no-underline pt-4.5 pb-3.5 px-8 text-lg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow sponsored noopener\">Learn more about Wise\u003C/a>\n\u003C/div>\n\n\n\n\u003Ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"housing\">How to find housing in Eindhoven\u003C/h2>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>If you have decided to move to Eindhoven, there are many different ways to find housing. You can independently search for accommodation or go through a real estate agent. \u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Students can browse the Eindhoven University of Technology&#8217;s \u003Ca href=\"https://www.tue.nl/en/education/become-a-tue-student/housing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">guide for internationals looking for housing\u003C/a>. You can also join groups on social media where users share rooms and apartments to rent in the city.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cdiv class=\"interal-link-wrapper\">\n            \u003Cdiv class=\"img-left\">\n            \u003Cimg loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/11/housing-netherlands.jpg\"  alt=\"#\" width=\"217\" height=\"144\">\n        \u003C/div>\n            \u003Ca href=\"https://www.expatica.com/nl/housing/housing-basics/housing-netherlands-139876/\" aria-label=\"Housing Housing in the Netherlands\">\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"content-right\">\n            \u003Cp class=\"category-name\">Housing\u003C/p>\n                \u003Cp class=\"guide-title-internal-link\">Housing in the Netherlands\u003C/p>\n        \u003Ca href=\"https://www.expatica.com/nl/housing/housing-basics/housing-netherlands-139876/\" class=\"internal-read-more\" aria-label=\"Read more\">Read more\u003C/a>\n    \u003C/div>\n    \u003C/a>\n\u003C/div>\n        \n\u003Cstyle>\n  .interal-link-wrapper {\n    display: flex;\n    gap: 40px;\n    border-bottom: 1px solid #DEDEDE;\n    border-top: 1px solid #DEDEDE;\n    padding: 54px 0 24px 0;\n    margin-bottom: 32px;\n  }\n  .interal-link-wrapper .img-left {\n    flex: 1 !important;\n  }\n  .interal-link-wrapper .content-right {\n    flex: 2 !important;\n  }\n\n  .content-right a {\n    text-decoration: none!important;\n  }\n  .category-name {\n    color: #00cba8 !important;\n    font-size: 17px !important;\n    line-height: 20px !important;\n    margin-bottom: 8px !important;\n    font-family: 'Grold-Medium', 'Nunito Sans', 'Arial', 'sans-serif'!important;\n    text-decoration: none;\n  }\n  .guide-title-internal-link {\n    color: #000000 !important;\n    font-size: 26px !important;\n    line-height: 31px !important;\n    font-family: 'Grold-Medium', 'Nunito Sans', 'Arial', 'sans-serif'!important;\n    margin-bottom: 32px !important;\n  }\n\n  /* Media query for screens with width less than 769 pixels */\n  @media screen and (max-width: 768px) {\n    .guide-title-internal-link {\n    color: #000000 !important;\n    font-size: 20px !important;\n    line-height: 24px !important;\n    font-family: 'Grold-Medium', 'Nunito Sans', 'Arial', 'sans-serif'!important;\n    margin-bottom: 32px !important;\n  }\n}\n  .internal-read-more {\n    color: #000000 !important;\n    font-size: 19px !important;\n    line-height: 23px !important;\n    -webkit-text-decoration: none;\n    text-decoration: none !important;\n    position: relative !important;\n    display: inline-block !important;\n    border-bottom: 1px solid #000000;\n    font-family: 'Grold-SemiLight', 'Nunito Sans', 'Arial', 'sans-serif'!important;\n  }\n\n  /* Media query for screens with width less than 769 pixels */\n  @media screen and (max-width: 768px) {\n        .interal-link-wrapper {\n            display: flex; /* Change from flex to block for mobile */\n            padding-top: 24px; /* Adjust padding for mobile */\n            padding-bottom: 0px;\n            gap: 0px;\n            margin-bottom: 16px; /* Adjust margin for mobile */\n        }\n        .interal-link-wrapper .img-left {\n          flex: 1!important;\n          width: 33.333333%;\n        }\n        .interal-link-wrapper .content-right {\n            flex: 2 !important; /* Remove flex property for mobile */\n            width: 66.666667%; /* Make both divs take full width for mobile */\n            margin-left: 30px;\n        }\n        .img-left img {\n            width: 33.333333%; /* Make the image take full width for mobile */\n            height: auto;\n            flex: 1; /* Maintain aspect ratio for mobile */\n        }\n        .category-name {\n            font-size: 14px !important; /* Adjust font size for mobile */\n        }\n        .guide-title-internal-link {\n            font-size: 18px !important; /* Adjust font size for mobile */\n            margin-bottom: 16px !important; /* Adjust margin for mobile */\n        }\n        .internal-read-more {\n            font-size: 16px !important; /* Adjust font size for mobile */\n            margin-bottom: 24px;\n        }\n    }\n\u003C/style>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Many online platforms list rental properties in Eindhoven. These include:\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"https://www.funda.nl/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Funda\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\n\n\n\n\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"https://housinganywhere.com/Netherlands?utm_source=expatica&amp;utm_medium=affiliate&amp;affiliate_partner_id=975640\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener sponsored nofollow\">HousingAnywhere\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\n\n\n\n\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"https://jdt8.net/c/?si=17650&amp;li=1767268&amp;wi=344199&amp;ws=\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener sponsored nofollow\">Huurwoningen\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\n\n\n\n\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"https://kamernet.nl/en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Kamernet\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\n\n\n\n\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"https://www.pararius.com/english\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Pararius\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\n\n\n\u003Ch3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"typical-accommodation\">Typical accommodation in Eindhoven\u003C/h3>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>As Eindhoven continues to expand its housing developments, many residents live in fairly new buildings. The city offers both apartments, especially towards \u003Cem>Centrum\u003C/em> (the city center), but also independent houses. \u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Students usually rent a room in an apartment or stay in university residences on campus. The housing market is competitive, so make sure you give yourself at least a few months for your accommodation search, whether renting or buying.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Ch3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"renting\">Renting in Eindhoven\u003C/h3>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Renting in Eindhoven is similar to \u003Ca href=\"https://www.expatica.com/nl/housing/renting/renting-a-property-in-the-netherlands-102925/\">renting in other Dutch cities\u003C/a>. Apartments and single-family homes are the most common type of property to rent, and prices depend on the property&#8217;s size, location, and condition. A standalone house in Elzent, just south of the city center, will fetch more than the more affordable Eikenburg, for example.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cfigure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\">\u003Cimg loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1800\" height=\"1200\" src=\"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/canal-eindhoven.jpg\" alt=\"Residential building next to a canal in Eindhoven\" class=\"wp-image-7576\" srcset=\"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/canal-eindhoven.jpg 1800w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/canal-eindhoven-300x200.jpg 300w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/canal-eindhoven-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/canal-eindhoven-768x512.jpg 768w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/canal-eindhoven-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/canal-eindhoven-380x253.jpg 380w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1800px) 100vw, 1800px\" />\u003Cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Photo: Alicja Ziaj/Unsplash\u003C/figcaption>\u003C/figure>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>When finding a property to rent, you first arrange to view the property, then express your interest and, if chosen, sign the contract. You must also typically pay a two-month deposit.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>When securing your rental property, you&#8217;ll likely need to transfer your deposit and first month&#8217;s rent internationally. Many expats use payment institutions like \u003Ca href=\"https://wise.com/nl/send-money/?utm_source=expatica-com&amp;utm_medium=affiliate&amp;utm_campaign=guides&amp;utm_content=be/moving/location/https://wise.com/be/account/?utm_source=expatica-com&amp;utm_medium=affiliate&amp;utm_campaign=guides&amp;utm_content=nl/moving/location/where-to-live-in-eindhoven-100616\">Wise\u003C/a> to send money to the Netherlands, as these services use the mid-market exchange rate—the real exchange rate without markup—alongside transparent fees. This can be particularly helpful when you need to manage EUR expenses while still holding funds in your home currency. Be sure to review the \u003Ca href=\"https://wise.com/nl/pricing/?utm_source=expatica-com&amp;utm_medium=affiliate&amp;utm_campaign=guides&amp;utm_content=nl/moving/location/https://wise.com/be/account/?utm_source=expatica-com&amp;utm_medium=affiliate&amp;utm_campaign=guides&amp;utm_content=be/moving/location/where-to-live-in-eindhoven-100616\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">fee structure\u003C/a> before making your transfer to understand the total cost.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Ch3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"buying\">Buying in Eindhoven\u003C/h3>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>If you plan to stay in the Netherlands long-term, you may consider \u003Ca href=\"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/housing/buying/buying-a-property-in-the-netherlands-100633/\">buying\u003C/a>. When purchasing a home in Eindhoven, the easiest way is to hire a real estate agent (\u003Cem>makelaar\u003C/em>). They can assist you when looking for a property and guide you through the entire buying process.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cdiv class=\"interal-link-wrapper\">\n            \u003Cdiv class=\"img-left\">\n            \u003Cimg loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/11/buying-a-home-in-the-netherlands.jpg\"  alt=\"#\" width=\"217\" height=\"144\">\n        \u003C/div>\n            \u003Ca href=\"https://www.expatica.com/nl/housing/buying/buying-a-property-in-the-netherlands-100633/\" aria-label=\"Housing Buying a home in the Netherlands\">\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"content-right\">\n            \u003Cp class=\"category-name\">Housing\u003C/p>\n                \u003Cp class=\"guide-title-internal-link\">Buying a home in the Netherlands\u003C/p>\n        \u003Ca href=\"https://www.expatica.com/nl/housing/buying/buying-a-property-in-the-netherlands-100633/\" class=\"internal-read-more\" aria-label=\"Read more\">Read more\u003C/a>\n    \u003C/div>\n    \u003C/a>\n\u003C/div>\n        \n\u003Cstyle>\n  .interal-link-wrapper {\n    display: flex;\n    gap: 40px;\n    border-bottom: 1px solid #DEDEDE;\n    border-top: 1px solid #DEDEDE;\n    padding: 54px 0 24px 0;\n    margin-bottom: 32px;\n  }\n  .interal-link-wrapper .img-left {\n    flex: 1 !important;\n  }\n  .interal-link-wrapper .content-right {\n    flex: 2 !important;\n  }\n\n  .content-right a {\n    text-decoration: none!important;\n  }\n  .category-name {\n    color: #00cba8 !important;\n    font-size: 17px !important;\n    line-height: 20px !important;\n    margin-bottom: 8px !important;\n    font-family: 'Grold-Medium', 'Nunito Sans', 'Arial', 'sans-serif'!important;\n    text-decoration: none;\n  }\n  .guide-title-internal-link {\n    color: #000000 !important;\n    font-size: 26px !important;\n    line-height: 31px !important;\n    font-family: 'Grold-Medium', 'Nunito Sans', 'Arial', 'sans-serif'!important;\n    margin-bottom: 32px !important;\n  }\n\n  /* Media query for screens with width less than 769 pixels */\n  @media screen and (max-width: 768px) {\n    .guide-title-internal-link {\n    color: #000000 !important;\n    font-size: 20px !important;\n    line-height: 24px !important;\n    font-family: 'Grold-Medium', 'Nunito Sans', 'Arial', 'sans-serif'!important;\n    margin-bottom: 32px !important;\n  }\n}\n  .internal-read-more {\n    color: #000000 !important;\n    font-size: 19px !important;\n    line-height: 23px !important;\n    -webkit-text-decoration: none;\n    text-decoration: none !important;\n    position: relative !important;\n    display: inline-block !important;\n    border-bottom: 1px solid #000000;\n    font-family: 'Grold-SemiLight', 'Nunito Sans', 'Arial', 'sans-serif'!important;\n  }\n\n  /* Media query for screens with width less than 769 pixels */\n  @media screen and (max-width: 768px) {\n        .interal-link-wrapper {\n            display: flex; /* Change from flex to block for mobile */\n            padding-top: 24px; /* Adjust padding for mobile */\n            padding-bottom: 0px;\n            gap: 0px;\n            margin-bottom: 16px; /* Adjust margin for mobile */\n        }\n        .interal-link-wrapper .img-left {\n          flex: 1!important;\n          width: 33.333333%;\n        }\n        .interal-link-wrapper .content-right {\n            flex: 2 !important; /* Remove flex property for mobile */\n            width: 66.666667%; /* Make both divs take full width for mobile */\n            margin-left: 30px;\n        }\n        .img-left img {\n            width: 33.333333%; /* Make the image take full width for mobile */\n            height: auto;\n            flex: 1; /* Maintain aspect ratio for mobile */\n        }\n        .category-name {\n            font-size: 14px !important; /* Adjust font size for mobile */\n        }\n        .guide-title-internal-link {\n            font-size: 18px !important; /* Adjust font size for mobile */\n            margin-bottom: 16px !important; /* Adjust margin for mobile */\n        }\n        .internal-read-more {\n            font-size: 16px !important; /* Adjust font size for mobile */\n            margin-bottom: 24px;\n        }\n    }\n\u003C/style>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>To get an idea of what types of properties are available to buy, check out sites like Funda. Several local companies also specialize in helping expats with the intricacies of Dutch mortgages.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"neighborhoods\">Neighborhoods in Eindhoven\u003C/h2>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Within the seven districts in Eindhoven, there are even more smaller neighborhoods. Fortunately, most areas are well connected by \u003Ca href=\"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/living/transportation/guide-to-public-transport-in-the-netherlands-100594/\">public transportation\u003C/a> or are a short bike ride away from each other. This means that you don&#8217;t necessarily have to live close to your work or school, but you can choose based on cost, amenities, and safety.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"centrum-bergen\">Centrum\u003C/h2>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>As its name suggests, Centrum is the heart and center of Eindhoven. The railway station is located here, and the lively and busy streets are full of shops and restaurants.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Within the central area of the city are smaller localities, such as Bergen. This is one of the town&#8217;s oldest neighborhoods. Its historic charm, trendy bars, and boutiques make it a sought-after location. Students often reside here thanks to its proximity to TU Eindhoven and the Design Academy.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cfigure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\">\u003Cimg loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1800\" height=\"1200\" src=\"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/centrum-eindhoven.jpg\" alt=\"Food stall in front of a glass building \" class=\"wp-image-7577\" srcset=\"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/centrum-eindhoven.jpg 1800w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/centrum-eindhoven-300x200.jpg 300w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/centrum-eindhoven-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/centrum-eindhoven-768x512.jpg 768w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/centrum-eindhoven-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/centrum-eindhoven-380x253.jpg 380w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1800px) 100vw, 1800px\" />\u003Cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Photo: Tayla Kohler/Unsplash\u003C/figcaption>\u003C/figure>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>There is always something to do in the city center, like visit a contemporary art exhibition at \u003Ca href=\"https://vanabbemuseum.nl/en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">The Van Abbemuseum\u003C/a> or stroll through the old town streets. \u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Public transportation and cycle paths run throughout Centrum, but there is less in the way of healthcare centers, primary schools, and playgrounds. Therefore, families with children usually reside in other districts. Furthermore, the central neighborhoods are some of the most expensive places to buy or rent property.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Overall, this is the place to be for a young professional or student who wants to be at the center of the hustle and bustle. It&#8217;s also a good option if you regularly commute to other cities, as it&#8217;s within easy reach of transport links.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"strijp\">Strijp\u003C/h2>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Located in the west of Eindhoven, Strijp is one of the city&#8217;s most unique and creative neighborhoods. It&#8217;s also a popular choice for expat families, as it&#8217;s home to the \u003Ca href=\"https://www.isecampus.nl/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">International School of Eindhoven\u003C/a> and multiple vast green spaces like the Philips de Jongh Park and Philips van Lenneppark.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>You&#8217;ll also find all your daily necessities in easy reach thanks to the neighborhood&#8217;s proximity to the city center and its facilities, including supermarkets, doctors, and pharmacies.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cfigure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\">\u003Cimg loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1800\" height=\"1200\" src=\"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/strijp-s.jpg\" alt=\"High-rise apartment building in Strijp-S, Eindhoven\" class=\"wp-image-7582\" srcset=\"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/strijp-s.jpg 1800w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/strijp-s-300x200.jpg 300w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/strijp-s-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/strijp-s-768x512.jpg 768w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/strijp-s-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/strijp-s-380x253.jpg 380w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1800px) 100vw, 1800px\" />\u003Cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Photo: Alex vd Slikke/Unsplash\u003C/figcaption>\u003C/figure>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>This neighborhood consists of smaller areas, such as Strijp-S, a more central location. In the early 20th century, this was Philips&#8217; industrial complex and manufacturing hub. These same buildings have been transformed into apartments, businesses, and a creative space. The district also has multiple art galleries, design studios, and startups. Each year, Dutch Design Week offers a rich cultural scene in the neighborhood, filling it with cinema, theater, and art installations.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Meanwhile, quieter, greener locations in this neighborhood include Merhooven. As it&#8217;s a convenient and interesting place to live in Eindhoven, prices can be high, but more affordable than in Centrum.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"woensel\">Woensel\u003C/h2>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Woensel, located north of the city center, is Eindhoven&#8217;s largest district. Housing in this residential area typically consists of apartments and single-family homes, which are usually more affordable compared to the rest of the city.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>An international student population resides in Woensel-Zuyd, as it&#8217;s close to the city center and universities. Woensel-Noord, on the other hand, is a better fit for families looking for roomy homes with green spaces. Another area, Blixembosch, offers more affordable homes and a vast choice of independent housing.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Overall, Woensel is ideal for students, families, and young professionals. It provides plenty of parks, sports centers, and primary and secondary schools. The variety of amenities and lower rental costs make this a popular choice for internationals moving to Eindhoven.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"stratum\">Stratum\u003C/h2>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Stratum is a charming neighborhood and popular residential area in southern Eindhoven. There is a variety of accommodation in the area, including older villas and more modern buildings. Parts of this neighborhood, such as Den Elzent, Tuindorp, Roosten, and Riel, provide single-family homes with abundant green spaces and parking.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cfigure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\">\u003Cimg loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1800\" height=\"1200\" src=\"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/stratum-eindhoven.jpg\" alt=\"Aerial view of an intersection in Stratum\" class=\"wp-image-7581\" srcset=\"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/stratum-eindhoven.jpg 1800w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/stratum-eindhoven-300x200.jpg 300w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/stratum-eindhoven-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/stratum-eindhoven-768x512.jpg 768w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/stratum-eindhoven-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/stratum-eindhoven-380x253.jpg 380w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1800px) 100vw, 1800px\" />\u003Cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Photo: Vishal/Unsplash\u003C/figcaption>\u003C/figure>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>These aspects of Stratum make it perfect for families, as well as its parks, supermarkets, and amenities. It&#8217;s also home to a range of community events – spend an afternoon strolling through Stadswandelpark or catch a live theater performance at \u003Ca href=\"https://www.parktheater.nl/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Parktheater Eindhoven\u003C/a>. If you&#8217;re into sports, don&#8217;t miss the \u003Ca href=\"https://www.eindhovensport.nl/zwemmen/tongelreep\">National Swimming Center of Tongelreep \u003C/a>and the neighborhood&#8217;s multiple sports parks.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Overall, costs throughout the district vary. The closer you are to the city center, the higher the prices. Because the whole city of Eindhoven is so well connected by bus, it is often more convenient to spend less on rent and live further away from Centrum. Stratum is a perfect area for families looking for a residential district that&#8217;s not too far from the heart of the city.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"gestel\">Gestel\u003C/h2>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Looking for a quiet residential neighborhood? Gestel, in southern Eindhoven, might be for you. Many people working at the High Tech Campus Eindhoven settle here to be close to work and to enjoy the other perks of the area. Within the district are micro-neighborhoods such as the popular Hanevoet and Bennekel.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cfigure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\">\u003Cimg loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1800\" height=\"1200\" src=\"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/recreatieplas-hanevoet.jpg\" alt=\"Recreatieplas Hanevoet: a small wooden pier going out into the lake\" class=\"wp-image-7580\" srcset=\"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/recreatieplas-hanevoet.jpg 1800w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/recreatieplas-hanevoet-300x200.jpg 300w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/recreatieplas-hanevoet-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/recreatieplas-hanevoet-768x512.jpg 768w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/recreatieplas-hanevoet-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/recreatieplas-hanevoet-380x253.jpg 380w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1800px) 100vw, 1800px\" />\u003Cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Photo: Partnair/Wikimedia Commons\u003C/figcaption>\u003C/figure>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Not only is Gestel quiet, safe, and peaceful, but it&#8217;s also easy to reach the city center – just under 15 minutes by bus. Local families and nature lovers adore the greenery of locations such as Recreatieplas Hanevoet, a lovely spot to take a walk in.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>All the necessary amenities, like doctors, schools, and pharmacies, are available in the district. Furthermore, it&#8217;s more affordable to rent or buy property here than in central Eindhoven.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"tongelre\">Tongelre\u003C/h2>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>East of the city center is the large district of Tonglere. This area is popular among expats and study-abroad students – it&#8217;s a short bike ride away from TU Eindhoven and home to Karpendonske Plas, where a \u003Ca href=\"https://www.parkrun.co.nl/karpendonkseplas/\">local Parkrun\u003C/a> takes place every Saturday morning.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cfigure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\">\u003Cimg loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1800\" height=\"1200\" src=\"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/tonglere-roundabout.jpg\" alt=\"A roundabout with modern art next to it\" class=\"wp-image-7583\" srcset=\"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/tonglere-roundabout.jpg 1800w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/tonglere-roundabout-300x200.jpg 300w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/tonglere-roundabout-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/tonglere-roundabout-768x512.jpg 768w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/tonglere-roundabout-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/tonglere-roundabout-380x253.jpg 380w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1800px) 100vw, 1800px\" />\u003Cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Photo: FaceMePLS/Wikimedia Commons\u003C/figcaption>\u003C/figure>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>This part of the city is well-connected to Centrum by bus, and it&#8217;s only a short bike ride to the main station, so it&#8217;s great for commuters. Its large quantity of boutiques, international restaurants, and museums make it a fun and vibrant part of Eindhoven to live in.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Two neighborhoods within Tonglere that are popular among students, young professionals, and expats, are Villapark and Karpen. However, property prices can be high in these areas.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"geldrop\">Geldrop\u003C/h2>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>While technically not in Eindhoven, the small town of Geldrop is a popular choice for people looking to save money on rent but keep easy access to the city. \u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>The municipality east of Eindhoven offers all necessary amenities, including its own hospital, schools, shops, and more. The entire town is surrounded by greenery, and it is famous for having streets named after characters and places from The Lord of the Rings.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cfigure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\">\u003Cimg loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1800\" height=\"1200\" src=\"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/geldrop.jpg\" alt=\"A bike next to a field on a sunny evening\" class=\"wp-image-7579\" srcset=\"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/geldrop.jpg 1800w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/geldrop-300x200.jpg 300w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/geldrop-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/geldrop-768x512.jpg 768w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/geldrop-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/1970/01/geldrop-380x253.jpg 380w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1800px) 100vw, 1800px\" />\u003Cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Photo: Kira Laktionov/Unsplash\u003C/figcaption>\u003C/figure>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>With just over 40,000 residents, this is an ideal space for a small-town feel with easy access to city life. It is only a seven-minute bus ride or a 20-minute bike trip from Geldrop to the central station in Eindhoven. \u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>If you live here, you can take daily walks in the nature preserve of Dommel or stroll by the \u003Cem>Kasteel Geldrop\u003C/em>, the local castle. Overall, this town has a residential, quaint, and peaceful atmosphere perfect for families. Few expats settle down here, so Geldrop is also ideal if you want to be immersed in the local culture.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"neighborhoods-to-avoid\">Neighborhoods to avoid in Eindhoven\u003C/h2>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Overall, Eindhoven is a safe place to live, scoring \u003Ca href=\"https://www.numbeo.com/crime/in/Eindhoven\">19.64\u003C/a> (very low) on Numbeo&#8217;s crowd-sourced crime perceptions survey. \u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>That being said, residents tend to avoid some parts of the city. For example, it is best to avoid spending time in the central train station at night. In addition, some areas, such as Vaartbroek, Kruisstraat, and Oud-Woensel, have a less favorable reputation among locals. It&#8217;s always good to be careful and aware of your surroundings in any city, but you&#8217;re unlikely to encounter much danger in Eindhoven.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"tips\">Tips on choosing a neighborhood in Eindhoven\u003C/h2>\n\n\n\n\u003Cp>Since Eindhoven has so many neighborhoods, choosing where to live may feel overwhelming. Each district has varying facilities, price points, and appeal. These tips can help you to make your choice easier:\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\u003Cul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n\u003Cli>Join expat groups on social media to ask for advice about living in Eindhoven.\u003C/li>\n\n\n\n\u003Cli>Understand what your priorities are. If you are looking to stay near one of the universities, you might want a neighborhood nearby. If you are a family with children, you may consider a quieter neighborhood like Eikenbur or Elzent. Daycare centers like \u003Ca href=\"https://partou.nl/en/childcare-locations?utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_source=expatica&amp;utm_campaign=kov_eindhoven&amp;utm_content=locations&amp;utm_term=discover\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener sponsored nofollow\">Partou\u003C/a> also have locations in Eindhoven.\u003C/li>\n\n\n\n\u003Cli>Remember that Eindhoven has excellent public transportation and is a bikeable city. Therefore, no matter where you choose to buy or rent, you will be able to reach where you need to go easily.\u003C/li>\n\n\n\n\u003Cli>Try visiting Eindhoven to get a feel for the city before officially deciding on a neighborhood.\u003C/li>\n\n\n\n\u003Cli>Many expats use \u003Ca href=\"https://wise.com/nl/account/?utm_source=expatica-com&amp;utm_medium=affiliate&amp;utm_campaign=guides&amp;utm_content=be/moving/location/https://wise.com/be/account/?utm_source=expatica-com&amp;utm_medium=affiliate&amp;utm_campaign=guides&amp;utm_content=nl/moving/location/where-to-live-in-eindhoven-100616\">Wise\u003C/a> (licensed in Belgium) for its multi-currency accounts and transparent international transfers to manage money across currencies, pay rent in euros and transfer funds internationally.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\n\n\n\u003Ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"useful-resources\">Useful resources\u003C/h2>\n\n\n\n\u003Cul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"https://www.thisiseindhoven.com/en/city-life/public-transportation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Public transportation in Eindhoven\u003C/a> – guide to getting around\u003C/li>\n\n\n\n\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"https://www.eindhoven.nl/en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Eindhoven municipal website\u003C/a> – information on living in Eindhoven\u003C/li>\n\n\n\n\u003Cli>University websites:\n\u003Cul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"https://www.tue.nl/en/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Eindhoven University of Technology\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\n\n\n\n\u003Cli>\u003Ca href=\"https://www.designacademy.nl/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Design Academy Eindhoven\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n","2025-12-11T16:29:09",{"value":589,"label":589},"Where to live in city","redesign_2026",null,"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/chiara-caporale-150x150.jpg","Chiara Caporale","chiara-caporale","\u003Cp>Growing up between Italy and the US, Chiara took her first flight at just three months old. She developed a passion for travel and now shares her stories about living in Italy through writing and video-making.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>Chiara works as a freelance writer and content creator and runs her own Italian teaching business.\u003C/p>\n",[],[],{"heading":599,"compareUrl":13,"note":600,"noteUrl":13},"Editor's top pick","Our picks are based on independent research covering plan value, coverage breadth, customer service, and claims experience.",{"title":602,"description":603,"robots":604,"canonical":610,"og_locale":611,"og_type":612,"og_title":585,"og_description":613,"og_url":610,"og_site_name":490,"article_publisher":614,"article_modified_time":615,"og_image":616,"twitter_card":619,"twitter_title":585,"twitter_description":603,"twitter_image":620,"twitter_site":621,"twitter_misc":622,"schema":624},"Where to live in Eindhoven: a guide for expats | Expatica","Discover life in the technology and design hub of the Netherlands and explore the best places to live in Eindhoven.",{"index":605,"follow":606,"max-snippet":607,"max-image-preview":608,"max-video-preview":609},"index","follow","max-snippet:-1","max-image-preview:large","max-video-preview:-1","https://www.expatica.com/nl/moving/location/where-to-live-in-eindhoven-100616/","en_US","article","Discover life in the technology and design hub of the Netherlands.","https://www.facebook.com/ExpaticaInternational/","2025-12-11T15:29:09+00:00",[617],{"url":618,"type":13,"width":13,"height":13},"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/11/eindhoven-1024x683.jpg","summary_large_image","https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/11/eindhoven.jpg","@Expatica",{"Est. reading time":623},"12 minutes",{"@context":625,"@graph":626},"https://schema.org",[627,645,650,658],{"@type":628,"@id":629,"url":610,"name":602,"isPartOf":630,"primaryImageOfPage":632,"image":634,"thumbnailUrl":620,"datePublished":635,"dateModified":615,"description":603,"breadcrumb":636,"inLanguage":638,"potentialAction":639,"accessibilityFeature":643},"WebPage","https://admin.expatica.com/nl/moving/location/where-to-live-in-eindhoven-100616/",{"@id":631},"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/#website",{"@id":633},"https://www.expatica.com/nl/moving/location/where-to-live-in-eindhoven-100616/#primaryimage",{"@id":633},"2014-05-16T12:17:15+00:00",{"@id":637},"https://www.expatica.com/nl/moving/location/where-to-live-in-eindhoven-100616/#breadcrumb","en-US",[640],{"@type":641,"target":642},"ReadAction",[610],[644],"tableOfContents",{"@type":646,"inLanguage":638,"@id":633,"url":620,"contentUrl":620,"width":647,"height":648,"caption":649},"ImageObject",1800,1200,"Eindhoven",{"@type":651,"@id":637,"itemListElement":652},"BreadcrumbList",[653,657],{"@type":654,"position":89,"name":655,"item":656},"ListItem","Home","https://admin.expatica.com/nl/",{"@type":654,"position":131,"name":585},{"@type":659,"@id":631,"url":656,"name":490,"description":660,"potentialAction":661,"inLanguage":638},"WebSite","Live. Work. Love.",[662],{"@type":663,"target":664,"query-input":667},"SearchAction",{"@type":665,"urlTemplate":666},"EntryPoint","https://admin.expatica.com/nl/?s={search_term_string}",{"@type":668,"valueRequired":669,"valueName":670},"PropertyValueSpecification",true,"search_term_string",[672],{"id":377,"name":379,"slug":380,"parent_slug":299},{"sizes":674,"alt_text":649},{"mobile-image":675,"medium_large":676,"1536x1536":677,"full":620},"https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/11/eindhoven-380x253.jpg","https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/11/eindhoven-768x512.jpg","https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/11/eindhoven-1536x1024.jpg",[679,686,693],{"title":680,"excerpt":681,"link":682,"imageUrl":683,"url":684,"category":685},"Primary schools in the Netherlands","Confused by the primary school system in the Netherlands? We explain how it works, from educational approaches to international options.","https://admin.expatica.com/nl/education/children-education/primary-schools-in-the-netherlands-150741/","https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2021/12/primary-school-netherlands-380x253.jpg","/nl/education/children-education/primary-schools-in-the-netherlands-150741/",{"name":33,"slug":34},{"title":687,"excerpt":688,"link":689,"imageUrl":690,"url":691,"category":692},"Higher education in the Netherlands: a guide to Dutch universities","The Netherlands is home to some of the world's top universities. Learn all about the different subjects available at Dutch institutions.","https://admin.expatica.com/nl/education/higher-education/universities-in-netherlands-240277/","https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/11/universities-in-netherlands-380x253.jpg","/nl/education/higher-education/universities-in-netherlands-240277/",{"name":180,"slug":181},{"title":694,"excerpt":695,"link":696,"imageUrl":697,"url":698,"category":699},"Child benefits in the Netherlands","You can claim different types of child benefits in the Netherlands, to help with the costs of child-rearing, schooling, and childcare.","https://admin.expatica.com/nl/living/family/child-benefits-netherlands-189747/","https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/11/child-benefits-netherlands-380x253.jpg","/nl/living/family/child-benefits-netherlands-189747/",{"name":33,"slug":34},[701,707,713],{"title":702,"link":703,"imageUrl":704,"url":705,"category":706},"Where to live in Haarlem","https://admin.expatica.com/nl/moving/location/where-to-live-in-haarlem-107009/","https://admin.expatica.com/nl/wp-co